    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Good morning, everybody. Welcome to the Lady Up America podcast. I am your host, Diane Canada. And so glad you're here today. We have got a special guest on the show. We are going to be welcoming in Senator Marsha Blackburn. Now, she has been serving the state of Tennessee in public service since the mid 90s. She started out as a representative here at the state level. Then she was sworn into the Tennessee State Senate in 1998. Then she went on to service in Congress. She represented the seventh congressional district here for Tennessee. And as of 2018, winning that election, she was sworn into the U.S. Senate in 2019. Prior to serving as publicly like she has so exemplary, she was actually a businesswoman. And she grew up in Laurel, Mississippi. She graduated from Mississippi State University. And she went on to have a very successful career in the retail world. And she started her own business, a marketing strategy firm. And so she's done a lot prior to coming into public service. I think it's so great that she was an entrepreneur first. So she really understands, she really understands us from so many angles. Many of you know that entrepreneurship is a big part of my heart. So I love that she had that experience prior to going into Congress and into the Senate. She's not a lifelong politician. She's also been married to Charles, a very sweet man who had the privilege of meeting. She has been married to Charles almost 50 years now. They've got two children, a son and a daughter, and they've got two grandsons, and they've got a granddaughter. So, family is a very, very big part of her life. One of the things I love about Marsha is that she makes it a point, a priority in her life, to fly home on weekends so that they can have family dinners. as often as possible. So she's really got her priorities straight. And she's just got so much fruit in her life to show for it. God says, you will know them by their fruit. And I'd say she's she's a walking example of that of that sentiment. So without further ado, I would love to welcome into the show Senator Marcia Blackburn. Thank you for carving out some time for our Lady of America community. I appreciate it very much. Yeah, we're going to dive right in because I know your time is limited. So I recently finished your book, The Mind of a Conservative Woman. Great book. Really enjoyed it. And although you've been serving in Tennessee for quite a while as our first are representative and then our senator in Washington, something I didn't know about you before reading the book was that you were from Laurel, Mississippi. And with the hometown show so popular right now, I just wonder if you're able to visit at all and see the transformations that Ben and Erin Napier are making. Oh,",
