    "turn_text": "flowers. Yeah, great conversation starters too, I'm sure. So my next question I wanted to dive into is we have so many women right now that are struggling with fear for the safety and well-being of their children. um, anger over, you know, the trajectory of our country, that mama bear instinct is really kicking in in a lot of women. And it's bringing out a lot of aggression. And something that you talked about so eloquently in your book too, is that we've got to be really mindful of not always being at war with everyone. I know this is so many things in our society right now are provoking that mama bear instinct and that aggression to want to protect our children. I know you mentioned in your book that Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher was one of your greatest inspirations and you know she had a quote that said it was something like if power is like a lady if you have to say it, then you don't have it, something along those lines. You always talk about being a happy warrior, and you encourage people. Every time I've seen you in group settings, we've had chances to talk briefly, but I've asked you recently, how are you holding up in Washington? And you just have a joy. You're like, I'm good, I'm good. So can you maybe share with women, what's your secret sauce in being a happy warrior in a culture right now that's provoking So much of this fear and anger.",
